# acc.merge(other) of Accumulator<T, 2> (milestone2.md, "The accumulator"): the running sums added,
# as add_2_2 (a node of the tree of the summation), and the sums of the magnitudes of the leading
# limbs added, rounded to nearest. The counts are added in the header. Both accumulators are
# objects: nothing comes from the program.
#
# The claims proposed for it in gen/kernels, which accumulator.py checks:
#   value:         s+v
#   requires:      normalized s
#   requires:      normalized v
#   requires:      nonneg a
#   requires:      nonneg c
#   ensures:       normalized t
#   ensures:       error t R c=3/(1-4*u) k=2 t=0
#   ensures:       rounded b nearest value=a+c
#   (needs rounded ... value=, which the generator does not have: see accumulator.py)
kernel:        acc_merge_2
input:         s = s0 s1
input:         a
input:         v = v0 v1
input:         c
output:        t = t0 t1
output:        b
min_precision: 3
source:        add_2_2 of two running sums, and the sum of the magnitudes (milestone2.md); JMP17 Alg. 6, bound from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   b, the sum of magnitudes, does not reach t0; it overflows (to +inf, its operands being nonnegative) only when a + c rounds above the largest number of T, and a radius computed from it is then +inf, the whole line

(t0, t1) = add_2_2(s0, s1, v0, v1)
b        = add(a, c)
